Learned: 
Some commands for users, navigation and file editing.
What operators are.
Up- and down arrows allow you to go through already used commands.

Commands used:
whoami - Tells who you are on the system.
echo - Outputs a specific text that is provided also if multiple words use "", if not just type the word.
ls - List what's in the current folder.
cd - Change directory so move in to another folder.
cat - Show the contents of a file.
pwd - Print working directory tell where you are or in which folder you're in.
find - Search for files by their name. For example: find -name passwords.txt .
grep - Searches inside for text. For example: grep "password123" passwords.txt .
& - Runs the command, but doesn't wait for it to finish. Good for commands that might take a while to finish.
&& - Runs both commands, but waits for the first command to finish first, before the next.
> - Used to redirect output. Takes the output of a command and sends it to a file. Will overwrite anything that exists in the file.
>> - Redirects output, but instead of overwriting data, it places it at the bottom of the file.

